"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[38574],{638574:e=>{e.exports="# fix-lints\n\nUse this when the user asks to fix lints, warnings, type errors, or\nsimilar findings across the notebook — regardless of which linter or\nlanguage server produced them.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Call `read-lints`. This returns lints from every diagnostic\n   provider that has reported on the notebook (e.g., Flint, the\n   Databricks language server's Ruff/TY checks, pyright). The result\n   includes:\n   - `lints`: array of findings; each has a `provider` and a `code`\n   - `summary.byCode`: count per rule code (across providers)\n   - `fixHints`: code → guidance string, only for codes that ship one\n   - `metadata.refreshedProviders` / `metadata.observedProviders`:\n     which providers were re-run vs. read-only\n   - `metadata.skippedCells`: counts of cells skipped during the\n     in-browser refresh (`nonPython` / `empty`)\n   - `metadata.errorCells`: cells where the headless lint threw,\n     with reason. If non-empty, the result is partial — surface\n     this to the user.\n   - `metadata.staleCells`: cells where the lint completed but the\n     result was discarded because the user edited the cell mid-run.\n     The snapshot for these cells is stale; if non-empty, suggest\n     re-running `read-lints` after a moment to get fresh results.\n\n2. If `summary.totalLints` is 0, tell the user there's nothing to fix\n   and stop.\n\n3. Group lints by (provider, code). For each group:\n   - If `fixHints[code]` exists, follow it as the authoritative fix\n     strategy.\n   - If not, fix using standard knowledge for that linter/rule\n     (e.g., Ruff codes have well-known meanings; type errors imply\n     adjusting types or values; deprecated APIs imply the modern\n     replacement).\n\n4. For each lint, edit the relevant cell using the existing cell-edit\n   tools. Reference cells by `cellId`. Apply the smallest change that\n   resolves the lint — do not refactor unrelated code.\n\n5. After applying edits, optionally call `read-lints` again to verify.\n   Report the diff to the user (e.g., \"Fixed 12 findings across 4\n   rules; 0 remaining\").\n\n## Constraints\n\n- Do not delete code unless the lint specifically calls for it.\n- Preserve cell language (`%sql`, `%python`, etc.) and magic commands.\n- If a lint requires user judgment (e.g., choosing between two valid\n  APIs, or a type narrowing that changes runtime behavior), ask the\n  user before applying.\n- Some providers (LSP-backed) only report on cells that have been\n  mounted in the editor. If `metadata.observedProviders` is missing\n  one you'd expect, or `metadata.errorCells` is non-empty, mention\n  this rather than silently assuming a clean bill.\n"}}]);
